From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiaoge-tou <85100527+Tiaoge-tou@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 23:18:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Hades pad: the layout editor reaches the Hades pad
 (long-press -)

Ports the nxnative fork's Hades pad customisation (Tiaoge-tou/nxnative 42d4a268) onto this fork's pad: the Silksong layout editor now serves the Hades pad too. Long-pressing the - key for 0.6 s opens the editor (drag to move, tap-select then - / + to scale 0.6-1.6x, restore defaults); the - key is a game key (boon info), so its press is held back while the watch runs: a tap is pulsed to the game on lift (70 ms), a hold opens the editor, a drag cancels, and the game never sees the hold. Geometry lives in its own NSUserDefaults key DmPadCustomHades, shared by all three Hades skins; hadesCenter/hadesR apply offset and scale uniformly across drawing, hit-testing and hot zones. The editor's bar, ring and accessors are shared by both pads; Silksong behaviour is unchanged.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: Hades II's pad gets the same per-player layout editor Silksong's has, synced from the nxnative fork at the owner's request; upstream's generic touch layout stays off for both games (their pads are independently adjusted).
Issue: Tiaoge-tou/NX2Apple PROJECT.md Phase 4

